## Claim
Text: "Anthony Weiner’s laptop contained proof Hillary Clinton & her associates are involved in child trafficking & paedophilia"
Claim date: October 18, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Anthony Weiner possess a laptop that was the subject of an FBI investigation in 2016?
Answer: Yes. According to FactCheck.org, "On Sept. 26, 2016, the FBI executed a search warrant on former Rep. Anthony Weiner's iPhone, iPad and laptop computer, and discovered 141,000 emails on the laptop that were potentially relevant to the FBI's closed investigation of Clinton." The FBI obtained an additional search warrant for the laptop on Oct. 30, 2016, to look for information related to the Clinton email investigation.

Source URL: https://www.factcheck.org/2018/08/clintons-emails-weiners-laptop-and-a-falsehood/

### What was the actual verified content of Anthony Weiner's laptop according to official law enforcement and court records?
Answer: According to official law enforcement records, including the June 2018 Justice Department Office of the Inspector General report and FBI documents, Anthony Weiner's laptop contained approximately 141,000 emails potentially relevant to the FBI's closed investigation into Hillary Clinton's use of a private email system while heading the State Department, along with 350,000 Clinton emails and 344,000 Blackberry communications discovered during NYPD forensic analysis. The FBI completed its review of these emails on Nov. 6, 2016, and Director James Comey concluded that "we have not changed our conclusions" regarding the Clinton email investigation. The official records contain no evidence of child trafficking, pedophilia, or any related material as claimed—there is no verified content on the laptop that substantiates the claim about Clinton and her associates being involved in such activities.

Source URL: https://www.factcheck.org/2018/08/clintons-emails-weiners-laptop-and-a-falsehood/

### Were any documents, emails, images, or other materials found on Anthony Weiner's laptop that referenced Hillary Clinton's involvement in child trafficking?
Answer: No. The search result makes no mention of any documents, emails, images, or other materials on Anthony Weiner's laptop referencing Hillary Clinton's involvement in child trafficking. According to the source, the laptop contained approximately 650,000 emails between Hillary Clinton and Huma Abedin related to the FBI's investigation into Clinton's use of a private email server during her tenure as Secretary of State. The laptop was originally seized in connection with an investigation into Weiner's alleged illicit relationship with a 15-year-old girl, but the Clinton/Abedin emails found on it pertained to the earlier concluded classified information investigation, not child trafficking. The FBI ultimately "did not change our conclusions that we expressed in July with respect to Secretary Clinton."

Source URL: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/hidden-legal-lessons-from-anthony-weiners-laptop-computer-stark

### Were any documents, emails, images, or other materials found on Anthony Weiner's laptop that referenced Hillary Clinton's involvement in paedophilia?
Answer: No. The search result indicates that the materials found on Anthony Weiner's laptop were emails from Hillary Clinton's State Department domain that had been copied to the laptop, which related to the investigation of Clinton's email usage. There is no mention of any documents, emails, images, or other materials referencing Clinton's involvement in paedophilia or child trafficking.

Source URL: https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2018/01/what-really-happened-with-andrew-mccabe-it-wasnt-conspiracy-fbi

### Were any documents, emails, images, or other materials found on Anthony Weiner's laptop that implicated any associate of Hillary Clinton in child trafficking or paedophilia?
Answer: Based on the search result, there is no mention of any documents, emails, images, or other materials found on Anthony Weiner's laptop that implicated any associate of Hillary Clinton in child trafficking or paedophilia. The laptop contained approximately 141,000 emails (and reportedly 350,000 in total) that were potentially relevant to the FBI's closed investigation into Clinton's use of a private email system while heading the State Department. The contents were related to official government communications and email system practices, not to child trafficking or paedophilia. As the source states, the FBI "reviewed all of the communications that were to or from Hillary Clinton while she was Secretary of State" and "have not changed our conclusions" regarding the email investigation.

Source URL: https://www.factcheck.org/2018/08/clintons-emails-weiners-laptop-and-a-falsehood/

### Has the FBI, U.S. Department of Justice, or any U.S. court ever stated that Anthony Weiner's laptop contained evidence linking Hillary Clinton to child trafficking or paedophilia?
Answer: No. The search results contain no such statement. The FBI documents describe the search of Weiner's laptop as part of an investigation into **Weiner's own** conduct—specifically "transmitting obscene material to a minor, sexual exploitation of children, and activities related to child pornography"—and the emails found on the laptop (approximately 340,000) were between Huma Abedin and Hillary Clinton related to Clinton's email server, not to child trafficking or paedophilia. As the FBI agent noted in the October 3, 2016 email, "I will not review any emails to which Anthony Weiner is not a party (such as emails between Ms. Abedin and Mrs. Clinton)," and there is no indication in any of the released documents that the FBI, DOJ, or any court linked Clinton to child trafficking or paedophilia based on the laptop's contents.

Source URL: https://www.judicialwatch.org/judicial-watch-fbi-documents-detail-weiner-laptop-clinton-email-find-just-before-the-2016-election/

### Who is the original source of the claim that Anthony Weiner's laptop contained proof of Hillary Clinton's involvement in child trafficking and paedophilia?
Answer: The original source of the claim, as reported by True Pundit, is **anonymous NYPD sources** (including a named "NYPD Chief") who told the outlet that the laptop contained evidence "to put Hillary (Clinton) and her crew away for life" and implicated her in sex crimes with children, money laundering, and other alleged offenses. The article states: "New York Police Department detectives and prosecutors working an alleged underage sexting case against former Congressman Anthony Weiner have turned over a newly-found laptop he shared with wife Huma Abedin to the FBI with enough evidence 'to put Hillary (Clinton) and her crew away for life,' NYPD sources told True Pundit."

Source URL: https://truepundit.com/breaking-bombshell-nypd-blows-whistle-on-new-hillary-emails-money-laundering-sex-crimes-with-children-child-exploitation-pay-to-play-perjury/

### Has any fact-checking organization, news outlet, or official government body debunked the claim that Anthony Weiner's laptop contained evidence of Hillary Clinton's involvement in child trafficking and paedophilia?
Answer: Yes, PolitiFact, a well-known fact-checking organization, explicitly debunked this type of claim in a November 4, 2016 fact-check, rating the claim "Pants on Fire!" (their lowest rating for falsehood). PolitiFact stated, "We could find no evidence that such a network exists; there is definitely no evidence that the FBI has confirmed it," noting that the claim relied on an anonymous post from an internet message board rather than any real evidence, and that the FBI itself stated it had "provided no comment, nor confirmed any investigation" beyond the existence of a letter to Congress.

Source URL: https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2016/nov/04/conservative-daily-post/evidence-ridiculously-thin-sensational-claim-huge-/

### What is the documented chain of custody and forensic analysis of Anthony Weiner's laptop, and what materials were officially confirmed to be on it?
Answer: Based on the search result, the documented chain of custody shows that on October 3, 2016, New York FBI agents executed a search warrant to obtain Weiner's iPhone, iPad, and laptop as part of an investigation into his alleged illicit relationship with a 15-year-old girl. The laptop appears to have been voluntarily turned over through cooperation with Weiner's attorneys. The original search warrant was limited to data related to Weiner's alleged conduct, but FBI agents discovered approximately 650,000 Clinton/Abedin emails on the laptop in "plain view" because Huma Abedin had reportedly used the laptop to back up her smartphone, inadvertently transferring the emails. The FBI then sought and obtained a second search warrant from a federal judge to review these emails. The FBI reviewed the 650,000 emails in approximately seven days, using processes including de-duplication, keyword searches, and forensic analysis of the hard drive. FBI Director James Comey confirmed in his October 28, 2016 letter to Congress the discovery of additional emails "between or among Hillary Clinton and Huma Abedin," and in his November 6, 2016 follow-up letter, stated they had "reviewed all of the communications that were to or from Hillary Clinton while she was Secretary of State" and "have not changed our conclusions that we expressed in July with respect to Secretary Clinton." The source contains no mention of any materials related to child trafficking or pedophilia involving Clinton or her associates.

Source URL: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/hidden-legal-lessons-from-anthony-weiners-laptop-computer-stark

### Did any credible, verifiable evidence emerge before or after October 18, 2020, that supported the claim that Anthony Weiner's laptop contained proof of criminal activity by Hillary Clinton or her associates?
Answer: The search result does not support the claim. The article discusses the legal issues surrounding Anthony Weiner's laptop and the FBI's discovery of Clinton/Abedin emails on it, but these emails were related to the previously concluded investigation into whether Hillary Clinton mishandled classified information using a private server — not child trafficking or paedophilia. Notably, FBI Director Comey stated in a November 6, 2016 letter to Congress: "we reviewed all of the communications that were to or from Hillary Clinton while she was Secretary of State... Based on our review, we have not changed our conclusions that we expressed in July with respect to Secretary Clinton." The article contains no mention of child trafficking or paedophilia involving Clinton or her associates, and the evidence actually undermines the claim rather than supporting it.

