### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is thoroughly refuted by multiple authoritative sources. Anthony Weiner's laptop, seized by the FBI in 2016, contained approximately 650,000 emails between Hillary Clinton and Huma Abedin related to the Clinton private email server investigation—not any evidence of child trafficking or paedophilia. FBI Director James Comey confirmed in his [November 6, 2016 letter to Congress](https://www.factcheck.org/2018/08/clintons-emails-weiners-laptop-and-a-falsehood/) that after reviewing all communications, the FBI "have not changed our conclusions" regarding the Clinton email investigation. The laptop was originally seized as part of an investigation into Weiner's own conduct (sexting with a minor), and no materials implicating Clinton or her associates in child trafficking or paedophilia were ever found. The claim originated from anonymous NYPD sources reported by [True Pundit](https://truepundit.com/breaking-bombshell-nypd-blows-whistle-on-new-hillary-emails-money-laundering-sex-crimes-with-children-child-exploitation-pay-to-play-perjury/), and [PolitiFact rated it "Pants on Fire!"](https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2016/nov/04/conservative-daily-post/evidence-ridiculously-thin-sensational-claim-huge-/)—their lowest rating for falsehood.